# I04.var10 prospective contract review — GO_CONSTRUCTION_ONLY

**Decision:** GO_CONSTRUCTION_ONLY for the frozen prospective design in `tmp/i04-var10-prospective-v100-20261008-03/contract.json` (13,393 bytes, SHA-256 `c00a8c11ec061e559ffaccf5c83b62e85cd6ab4cedd4a39316877a08bc4cbb69`). This authorizes construction and later independent static review of a new I04.var10 package only. It does not authorize SSH preflight, native calculation, acceptance, catalog edits, or Git writes. The accepted I04.var03 parent and its checkers were not rerun.

I independently reviewed the pinned source, manual, precedent, catalog archives, event chronology, full proposed log and report oracle. The original read-only audit `tmp/i04-var10-independent-contract-audit-v100-20261008.py` is 11,375 bytes, SHA-256 `08578839fcd56439d5d86ddccb5e501a9d00b0d0169134f3877bde2da0e3d09f`, and read-only. Root captured its single actual execution in `tmp/i04-var09-root-review-proofs-v100-20261008/i04-var10-independent-contract-audit-20261008T124545831487Z-b71cd3a2/receipt.json` (1,368 bytes, SHA-256 `58a773c3d10d8fdb99912067301679e88eccc3b471e38a0d6b361b7771b155c8`): integer exit 0, empty original stderr, stable method pins, and original stdout SHA-256 `7fad0f73fa8ffdd2a57514008f048c61b530e445340f0d1962970d09db037b48`. The root generator capture also exited 0 with empty original stderr and stable method pins: `tmp/i04-var09-root-review-proofs-v100-20261008/i04-var10-prospective-generation-v5-20261008T124328302685Z-b60e0042/receipt.json` (1,358 bytes, SHA-256 `fd5c8a19961e5515315f1d87b6e0c1b5d406232458cf101cf16b3e66dafb5131`). Neither proof made a native call or created a case package.

The six exact source-cell changes are `PDESC`, Control `SIMPE/RCEND` 36→11, both explicit ResultCollection `RCEND` 36→11, and BETWEEN `TFDT` 0.5→2. The complete h20 OperationProfile row is a seventh, explicit deletion; h8 remains. The resulting prospective source has 34 tables, 21 populated rows, and 211 authored cells. The deletion is necessary to avoid a known converter risk: D12.var03 v1.0.0 retained post-horizon h20/h32 rows and received `#204`, while its corrected version and the accepted E02.var03 hour-11 case removed later rows. The frozen exact source delta is 2,071 bytes, SHA-256 `7d53ed9c457bd0a8927e6d90bde0fbded6834ceea51911712a753347f0c620c4`; the proposed native export topology of 34 tables, 39 rows, and 395 cells remains a predeclared test, not observed output.

The installed SIMLOX manual SHA-256 `39427027c46809a9ce9ebcb9be04e7396d96746e42a6f8c7c0ba2ddc294ef8a3` documents ready-pool BETWEEN transfer and `TFDT` as departure-to-arrival delay (physical pages 225, 480–481). It says the simulation ends at `SIMPE` and state results are interval averages with per-result collection limits (pages 230–231). It does **not** establish native accounting for a transfer pending at the horizon. The contract therefore makes a falsifiable, bounded prediction: numeric ID 0 departs at 10.5, its calculated arrival is 12.5, and an hour-11 valid simulation has no arrival or second mission. The complete proposed log is exactly 61 physical lines and 53 timed records, including numeric header `11` and the accepted parent event prefix through transfer-out; `log-oracle.json` is 4,758 bytes, SHA-256 `91f9981956a28414feeea056d963eccd4fe59904ec19b28c988fafc876d24b64`. Any extra end diagnostic, arrival, reorder, or altered identity is NO_GO under this contract.

The complete prospective four-table report is 1,244 cells: one description, eleven summary cells, and 22 half-hour System plus 22 Stock rows over `[0,11)`. Every predicted row value is generated from the predeclared h7–10 assignment, h8–10 flight, h7–8 reservation and h10.5–12.5 transfer interval, with declared zero/null rules. Accepted parent first-22 rows corroborate the result but do not supply the generated values. System-hour integrals are ready 15.5, assigned 6, flying 4, reserved 2 and in-unit 21.5; the final bin has one in-unit/ready system and one proposed in-transit system. The complete `report-oracle.json` is 35,690 bytes, SHA-256 `bd5c7d0e8993b3aa7866b4900782f30a7dbaacb1a0af5b58650c172ac0e4ef7f`. Its terminal null and summary fields are **prospective predictions**. An observed different value requires NO_GO and a new reviewed contract; it cannot be fit to the output.

The converter gate requires errors 0, warnings exactly `108,126`, notes 0, exact Input/Output/File paths and original streams. The proposed diagnostic `File:` line is the forward-slash absolute path ending `model.sxi`, 121 ASCII bytes, below the 199-byte bound. Its short physical run directory, `tmp/native-runs/i04v10-v100-20261008-01`, must remain absent and free of reparse ancestors before any dispatch. Construction must preserve the distinct catalog 499 local CRLF and base Git LF byte identities and all accepted parent source/raw pins. The earlier retained-profile draft, decoded-only syntax failure, wrong-manual/header draft, and unexecuted wrong-File/copied-report draft remain excluded history; none is positive evidence.

**Next gates:** independent review of child source, full strict reader, validator and runner; original PURE proof and actual zero-native SSH preflight; then a fresh receipt-bound independent GO_PRELAUNCH before any one-time native dispatch. A converter rejection, missing report, or any strict log/report mismatch remains a preserved NO_GO. This review makes no general claim about terminal transfers, later arrival, GUI behavior, or another engine.
